    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Opening a project now shows its invoices, their total, and a form to add a new invoice by amount. `bin/e2e` builds and runs, and both Playwright tests pass.\n\nYour request said \"OfficeFloor server\", but this codebase and `CLAUDE.md` are Spring Boot. I followed the code, so the server side is ordinary Spring.\n\n**What's new**\n- **Projects list:** each row has an \"Open\" link (`project-open-<id>`) that goes to the project's own page at `/projects/<id>`. That page doesn't appear in the nav bar.\n- **Project page:** shows the project's name and client, the invoices table (`invoice-row-<id>` / `invoice-amount`), and the total in the table footer (`project-invoices-total`). Amounts show two decimals, and the total is added up in whole cents so rounding can't creep in.\n- **Add invoice:** the form (`invoice-form-amount`, `invoice-form-submit`) accepts only amounts above zero with at most two decimal places. The server and database enforce the same rule.\n\n**Server and database**\n- `V4__create_invoice.sql` adds an `invoice` table: an id, the project it belongs to, and an amount stored as an exact decimal.\n- New endpoints:\n  - `GET /api/projects/{id}` returns one project.\n  - `GET /api/projects/{id}/invoices` lists that project's invoices.\n  - `POST /api/projects/{id}/invoices` adds an invoice.\n  - An unknown project id returns 404.\n- The test reset and seed endpoints now handle invoices.\n\n**Worth knowing**\n- When a project has no invoices, the page shows \"No invoices yet.\" and no total, rather than a total of 0.00.\n- Creating an invoice doesn't write an audit record. The test doesn't expect one, and creating clients or projects doesn't write one either.\n- I changed the app-wide router setup so route parameters are passed straight into page components (`app.config.ts`).\n\nThe invoice files are in `src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/invoice/` and `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/invoices/`. The project page is `features/projects/project-detail.ts`.",
